---
import InteriorLayout from '../layouts/InteriorLayout.astro';
---

<InteriorLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Juneteenth Conference 2026"
  description="Privacy policy for JuneteenthConf. How we collect, use, and protect your information."
  current=""
  heroTitle="Privacy Policy"
  heroSubtitle="How we handle your information"
  heroAccent="gold"
>
  <section class="interior-section">
    <div class="interior-content">
      <div class="reveal-stagger">

        <p class="reveal effective-date">Effective date: April 13, 2026</p>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <p class="policy-intro">
            JuneteenthConf, Unl. ("JuneteenthConf," "we," "our") operates juneteenthconf.com and
            related subdomains. This policy explains what information we collect, why we collect it,
            and your rights regarding it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">1. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3 class="policy-subheading">Information you provide</h3>
          <p class="policy-text">When you sign up for our newsletter, register for the conference, or submit a volunteer or speaker inquiry, we collect:</p>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li>Name and email address</li>
            <li>Phone number (volunteer form, optional)</li>
            <li>Preferences and notes you choose to share</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="policy-subheading">Analytics data</h3>
          <p class="policy-text">
            We use <strong>Umami</strong>, a privacy-first analytics platform hosted on our own
            infrastructure at <code>analytics.juneteenthconf.com</code>. Umami does not use cookies
            and does not collect personally identifiable information. It collects:
          </p>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li>Page URL and referrer</li>
            <li>Browser type and operating system (aggregated)</li>
            <li>Country-level location (derived from IP, not stored)</li>
            <li>Session duration and page interactions</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="policy-text">
            No persistent identifiers are stored on your device. No data is shared with third parties.
            No cookie consent banner is required.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li>Send conference updates, speaker announcements, and registration information</li>
            <li>Coordinate volunteer participation</li>
            <li>Improve the website and understand visitor behavior (analytics only)</li>
            <li>Respond to inquiries</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="policy-text">We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">3. Email Communications</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">
            We manage our mailing lists using <strong>Listmonk</strong>, self-hosted on our own
            infrastructure at <code>mail.juneteenthconf.com</code>. Email delivery is handled via
            Microsoft Azure Communication Services. Your email address is used only for
            JuneteenthConf communications and is never shared with third parties.
          </p>
          <p class="policy-text">
            Every email includes an unsubscribe link. You may also request removal at any time by
            emailing <a href="mailto:info@juneteenthconf.com">info@juneteenthconf.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">4. Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">
            Newsletter subscriber data is retained until you unsubscribe or request deletion.
            Analytics data is retained for 24 months in aggregate form and contains no personal
            identifiers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">5. Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">Depending on your location, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li>Request correction or deletion of your data</li>
            <li>Opt out of email communications at any time</li>
            <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="policy-text">To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@juneteenthconf.com">info@juneteenthconf.com</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">6. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">We use the following services in operating this site:</p>
          <ul class="policy-list">
            <li><strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> — hosting, email delivery infrastructure</li>
            <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — static site deployment via GitHub Actions</li>
            <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — font files served locally; no Google requests at runtime</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">
            We may update this policy as our practices change. Material changes will be noted with
            an updated effective date. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes
            acceptance of the revised policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal policy-block">
          <h2 class="policy-heading">8. Contact</h2>
          <p class="policy-text">
            JuneteenthConf, Unl.<br />
            Fiscally sponsored by YPOC Harrisburg (501(c)(3))<br />
            <a href="mailto:info@juneteenthconf.com">info@juneteenthconf.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</InteriorLayout>

<style>
  .interior-section {
    padding: 60px 24px 80px;
    background: #231c2d;
  }
  .interior-content {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .effective-date {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.35);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .policy-intro {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.65);
    line-height: 1.75;
    border-left: 3px solid rgba(212, 168, 67, 0.4);
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .policy-block {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }
  .policy-heading {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: #D4A843;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 168, 67, 0.15);
  }
  .policy-subheading {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.8);
    margin: 20px 0 8px;
  }
  .policy-text {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.6);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .policy-text a {
    color: #D4A843;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .policy-text a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .policy-text code {
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.08);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.7);
  }
  .policy-list {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.6);
    line-height: 1.75;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .policy-list li { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .policy-list strong { color: rgba(240, 237, 230, 0.8); }
</style>
